{
  "id": "electrical-stimulation",
  "term": "electrical stimulation",
  "definition": "Electrical stimulation is a method that delivers low-intensity direct or alternating electrical current through electrodes placed on the scalp or skin. In transcranial forms, the current is thought to alter brain cell activity and communication, and different forms can influence cortical processing in ways that may affect behavior and performance on cognitive or motor tasks.",
